{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CapacityLog"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The log is a collection of its elements, from the oldest to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newest. It can be iterated, and the elements can be accessed by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their position, where the oldest element is at position zero."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["for transition in log {","    print(transition)","}","","let oldest = log.first","let secondNewest = log[log.count - 2]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The log can be encoded when its elements can, and decoded when they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be decoded. It is saved with its max capacity, so a decoded log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"goes on dropping its oldest elements like the log encoded. The keys"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", left out for a log without max capacity, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"elements","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with the elements from the oldest to the newest."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The log is implemented with the Apple Swift Collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deque and should be performant."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MiamiStateMachine\/documentation\/MiamiStateMachine\/CapacityLog\/init(capacity:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated"